S("_MgJJpqxcn8","How to Get a Vibey Filtered Drum Sound (ambient / indie mixes)",
 "filtered-vibey-drum-bus-lowpass-1k-boxy-mid-tube-drive-borrowed-verb-sends-automated-long-plate-throws",
 "Filtered 'vibey' drum bus: low-pass the kit down to ~1 kHz with a 500 Hz-1 kHz boxy boost, add gentle tube saturation, send it to reverbs already in the mix (a pitched/chorused verb and a low-cut, EQ'd, chorused hall), then automate sends into an 8 s+ plate (low cut ~500-600 Hz) only at phrase ends, and ride the bus volume up into the end",
 "Turn a plain drum kit, loop or recorded drums into a soft, dark, spacious drum layer that sits behind ambient pads. Delta vs drum-groove cluster (lo-fi groove, sparse drums, organic downtempo groove): this is the processing chain and send automation, not pattern writing, and it reuses existing return reverbs so the drums share the mix's space.",
 ["Any drum source (kit, loop, drum sampler or synthesized drums)","EQ/filter, saturator (tube style), 2-3 reverb returns, a gain/utility device for automation"],
 [("drums","audio/midi","Drum track or loop",True),("existing_returns","reverb sends","Reverb returns already used on other parts of the mix",False)],
 [("filtered_drums","audio","Dark, filtered drum bus with shared space and phrase-end reverb throws")],
 ["The low-pass filter is the main effect; saturation is secondary (any tube/tape saturator works).","Reverb throws come in only at certain hits or phrase ends, not on every hit.","Drums still enter early (~8 counts / ~12 s); no rapid clicking rolls or stutters (Matt's preference).","Automate a gain/utility device instead of the fader so the fader stays free."],
 [("Start from a plain, fairly thin drum sound (kit preset, loop or synthesized drums).","Drum source","Reference before processing"),
  ("Insert an EQ: low-pass the top end down to roughly 1 kHz and add a broad boost between ~500 Hz and 1 kHz for a meaty, boxy mid-range.","EQ","Drums sound dark and filtered with body in the mids"),
  ("Add a gentle tube-style saturation/distortion (tone controls minimal).","Saturator","More warmth and character, no harsh grit"),
  ("Send the drums to reverb returns already set up for other parts (e.g. a vocal verb with pitch-shift/chorus/width into 100% wet reverb). Keep it low and try what's there before making new ones.","Send/return","Drums share the mix's space"),
  ("Send to a hall return that has a chorus and heavy EQ on the wet signal itself (low and high cut), so the reverb is filtered too.","Hall reverb return + chorus + EQ","Fuller space that stays dark"),
  ("Create an 'accent' return: a plate with 8 s+ decay and low cut ~500-600 Hz. Automate the drum send to it so it only opens at the ends of some bars/phrases, and leave it open longer near the end of a section.","Plate reverb + send automation","Long tails stretch out only on chosen hits"),
  ("Automate the drum bus volume (gain/utility device) to rise gently towards the end of a section to build energy.","Gain automation","Drum energy grows without touching the fader"),
  ("A/B the bus with all plugins off and on, alone and in the full mix.","A/B","Clear 'vibe' difference, drums sit behind pads")],
 ["Drum bus spectrum shows a roll-off above ~1 kHz with a mild 500 Hz-1 kHz bump.","The long-plate send is non-zero only at automated phrase-end spots.","Drums still enter by ~12 s; no rolls or rapid clicks are added."],
 ["drums","drum-bus","low-pass","filter","saturation","reverb-send","automation","ambient","lo-fi"])

S("aBiz2axINMA","How to Create Monaural Beats in Ableton Live (Step-By-Step Tutorial)",
 "monaural-beat-two-fixed-sines-or-tremolo-at-entrainment-rate-on-playable-pad-speaker-safe",
 "Speaker-safe brainwave layer in a DAW: either two fixed-frequency sines a few Hz apart summed in mono (e.g. carrier + 8 Hz for alpha), or a tremolo (auto-pan set to tremolo, high amount, ~40% shape) at the entrainment rate on a playable pad so chords themselves pulse, optionally with the sine pair underneath",
 "Build a monaural beat that works on speakers as well as headphones, and turn ordinary pads into the entrainment source. Delta vs brainwave cluster (isochronic layer as its own track, binaural per-ear tones): this one puts a tremolo at the target rate directly on a playable pad/chord track and uses an in-mono two-sine pair instead of per-ear panning.",
 ["Any synth that can make a sine at a fixed frequency (e.g. FM synth in fixed mode)","A tremolo or auto-pan device that can run at a set Hz rate","An instrument/chain rack or two tracks"],
 [("target_rate_hz","number","Entrainment rate, e.g. 8 Hz (alpha), 4-8 theta, 1-4 delta",True),("carrier_hz","number","Carrier frequency; pick a note of the track's key",True),("pad","instrument","Sustained pad (not short or fast-changing)",False)],
 [("monaural_layer","audio","Summed two-sine beat or tremolo-pulsed pad at the target rate")],
 ["Carrier frequency should be a note in the track's key (calculate the Hz of that note); the 432 Hz framing in the video is optional, not required.","Use a sustained, stable pad for the tremolo; short or fast-changing sounds blur the pulse.","Keep the effect gentle and test it on yourself first before sharing; make no health claims.","Steady pulse and steady pitch; no random rate or pitch modulation (Matt's preference)."],
 [("Option A: load a sine synth, set the oscillator to fixed frequency at the carrier (a key note).","Sine synth (fixed mode)","Pure steady tone"),
  ("Put it in a rack/group, duplicate the chain, and set the second sine to carrier + target rate (e.g. +8 Hz). Keep both centred (mono).","Instrument rack","An audible amplitude 'wobble' at the target rate even on speakers"),
  ("Check: mute one chain and the wobble disappears; both together give the monaural beat.","Mute A/B","Beat confirmed"),
  ("Option B: on a pad or chord track, add a tremolo (auto-pan in tremolo mode), raise the amount high, set shape ~40%, and set the rate to the target Hz (e.g. 8 Hz).","Tremolo/auto-pan","Pad pulses at the entrainment rate"),
  ("Turn off fixed pitch so the instrument plays normally; play chords and melodies so the whole harmony pulses.","Pad + tremolo","Composable entrainment layer instead of a bare sine"),
  ("Add reverb after the tremolo and, if wanted, keep the Option A sine pair quietly underneath.","Reverb + layer","Pulse stays clear but softened"),
  ("Optionally copy the same tremolo onto other tracks of a meditation piece, then test-listen at length before sharing.","Copy device","Consistent rate across the track")],
 ["The two sines differ by exactly the target rate (e.g. 432 vs 440 Hz = 8 Hz).","The tremolo rate equals the target rate in Hz, not a tempo-synced value.","The pulse is audible on mono/speaker playback."],
 ["brainwave","monaural-beat","isochronic","tremolo","auto-pan","entrainment","pad","ableton"])

S("64H_K7rosSo","How I Produce a Sleep Meditation Track in Ableton Live (Step-By-Step Tutorial)",
 "sleep-descent-arrangement-40-50bpm-descending-lines-staggered-fade-ins-lowpass-recede-key-tuned-binaural-notch",
 "Sleep/wind-down ambient arrangement at 40-50 BPM: loop-first sketch of pads, strings and soft plucks playing descending in-key lines, then arrange with slow volume fade-ins per layer, automated low-pass (and an EQ low cut scaled in when layers collide with the bass) so the track 'moves away', a long master fade, and a binaural/monaural pair tuned to the key's root with a narrow EQ notch carved for it in other parts",
 "Arrange a long sleep or meditation track whose energy only goes down. Delta vs arrangement-ambient cluster (44-bar ambient shape, bite-sized sections, frequency-range layering): a descent-only arc where filters close and the mix recedes over time, plus a key-root-tuned brainwave pair with notch carving. Use it as the arc for slow brainwave pieces.",
 ["A DAW with volume/utility and filter automation","Pads, strings, a soft pluck/woodwind, a sine generator"],
 [("length_min","number","Target length (10-60 min; longer allows slower fades)",True),("key","string","Key/scale, e.g. E minor",True),("target_rate_hz","number","Brainwave rate, e.g. 3-4 Hz delta (start ~8 Hz for wind-down and ramp down)",False)],
 [("sleep_track","audio/arrangement","Descending, receding ambient arrangement with an embedded key-tuned beat")],
 ["Tempo 40-50 BPM (around resting heart rate); avoid upward-lifting melodies.","Mono glide is optional and must stay short and deliberate, a steady slide between notes, not wobble; no random pitch or randomised notes (Matt's preference).","No drums are required for a sleep piece; if drums are used elsewhere in a set, Matt's early-drums rule applies to beat-led tracks.","Make no health claims; test-listen before sharing."],
 [("Set the tempo to 40-50 BPM.","Transport","Slow pulse near resting heart rate"),
  ("Build a loop first: a deep pad foundation with reverb, then a strings line, a warm woodwind and a soft pluck with delay/echo, each playing simple descending in-key lines (e.g. E-D-A-E). Use the scale highlight to stay in key.","Instruments + reverb/delay","A calm loop where every melody moves down"),
  ("Lay the layers out along the timeline and give each a volume (utility) fade-in curve; bring in the loudest or most bass-heavy parts more slowly.","Gain automation","Layers enter gradually without jumps"),
  ("Make the mix 'move away' over time: automate low-pass cutoff down on bright layers (e.g. pluck, poly pad).","Auto filter","Track gets duller and more distant"),
  ("Where a layer's lows collide with the bass, keep an EQ low cut at a fixed frequency and automate the device's amount/scale in as the layer enters.","EQ + scale automation","Bass stays clear as layers arrive"),
  ("Lower individual layers that feel strong in the ear, then add a very long master fade-out (stretch over the full length).","Master utility","Whole piece recedes slowly"),
  ("Add the brainwave layer: a sine at the key's root (e.g. E5 659 Hz) and a second at root minus the rate (656 Hz = 3 Hz); pan left/right for binaural or keep centred for monaural. Set it just loud enough that you notice when it's muted.","Fixed sine pair","Gentle beat at the target rate"),
  ("Carve a narrow EQ notch at the tone frequency in competing parts, and give the tone its own slow fade-in and fade-out.","EQ notch + fades","Tone sits clearly without masking"),
  ("Export, listen at the intended time (e.g. that evening), then adjust lengths, rate and levels.","Export + review","Notes for the next revision")],
 ["Tempo is between 40 and 50 BPM.","Low-pass cutoff on bright layers trends downward across the arrangement, and master gain ends lower than it starts.","The sine pair differs by the target rate and the root matches the key; competing parts have a notch at that frequency."],
 ["arrangement","ambient","sleep","meditation","fade-in","filter-automation","brainwave","binaural","descending-melody"])
